<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Telekom details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Telekom details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				   63,100 vs 59,600</p>
<p>Increase in inventory, other own</p>
<p>    capital costs				  7,400 vs  5,400</p>
<p>    Goods and services purchased	    10,200 vs  9,500</p>
<p>    Personnel costs			     18,800 vs 18,500</p>
<p>    Depreciation				  17,700 vs 15,400</p>
<p>    Other operating expenses		   9,500 vs  9,600</p>
<p>    Net financial expense			7,700 vs  8,200</p>
<p>    Group income on ordinary activities    6,600 vs  3,800</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss			   2,500 vs  1,300</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit			 4,100 vs  2,500</p>
<p>    Taxes					    2,200 vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Net income before minority interests   1,900 vs  n/a</p>
<p>Loss applicable to minority</p>
<p>    shareholders				   0,100 vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Net income				     1,800 vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Group workforce (on Dec 31)	    201,000 vs 213,500</p>
<p>Investment:</p>
<p>     Financial assets			    5,600 vs   2,000</p>
<p>     Capital expenditure			15,700 vs  17,000</p>
<p>    Net income according to U.S. GAAP	2,600 vs   n/a</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>     German GAAP				    0.83 vs n/a marks</p>
<p>     U.S. GAAP					2.60 vs n/a marks</p>
<p>     DVFA/SG					  1.13 vs n/a marks</p>
<p>    Shareholder's equity on Dec 31	  46,600 vs 24,700</p>
<p>    Cash flow from operating activities   22,300 vs 23,700</p>
<p>    Financial debt (on Dec 31)		98,600 vs 110,500</p>
<p>Details of first quarter 1997:</p>
<p>    Revenue					 16,300 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Income before taxes			  2,200 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Workforce (at end March)		 199,000 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Financial debt (at end March)	   96,000 vs n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German telecommunications group is Deutsche Telekom AG. The data for 1995 are adjusted to reflect tax changes in 1996 in order to present a comparable basis.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 145</p>
</text>
